item.description:
Target: Windows x86-64 (first integer arg in ecx). Reverse this function to equivalent C.

func:
    xor     eax, eax
    xor     r8d, r8d
.loop:
    mov     edx, r8d
    imul    edx, edx
    add     eax, edx
    inc     r8d
    cmp     r8d, ecx
    jl      .loop
    ret

What does func compute, in terms of its single parameter?

Answer:
int func(int n) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        sum += i * i;
    }
    return sum;
}

1. eax (return value) and r8d (loop counter i) are both zeroed before the loop starts.
2. Each iteration computes i*i into edx via imul edx, edx, then adds it into the running total eax.
3. inc r8d / cmp r8d, ecx / jl .loop implements for (i = 0; i < n; i++), comparing against ecx -- the Windows x64 first-argument register n -- so func returns the sum of squares from 0 to n-1.
